    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0287" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg283"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/197: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-27T17:00:00+08:00">February 27, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 27—2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>325. Reference my 234, February 10, 6 p.m.<anchor n="73" xml:id="d363-f1"/> last
                    paragraph. Following an assurance given me some days ago, the Japanese
                    authorities have now announced that facilities will be given for the removal of
                    foreign cargo from the Chinese wharves and warehouses in question in the area
                    north of the Creek beginning March 1. This is not the end of our problems but we
                    are slowly making some headway.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
